00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:27.047
- The thing which attracted me to Google,

00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:29.658
and to Internet in general,

00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:32.826
is that it's a great equalizer.

00:00:32.826 --> 00:00:37.360
And so, to me, always been
struck by the fact that

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.670
Google Search worked the same
as long as you had access

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.295
to a computer with connectivity,

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:45.004
if you were a rural kid anywhere

00:00:45.004 --> 00:00:47.673
or if you were a professor
in Stanford or Harvard.

00:00:47.673 --> 00:00:51.840
And to me, I want Google to
strive to push to do that,

00:00:53.043 --> 00:00:57.345
not just build technology
for certain segments,

00:00:57.345 --> 00:01:01.530
for me it matters that we drive technology

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.501
as an equalizing force,

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.613
as an enabler to everyone
around the world.

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:07.857
- I think the best thing that you can do

00:01:07.857 --> 00:01:11.005
is create a product or
service that empowers people.

00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:12.905
That's what we do as entrepreneurs.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.619
We see a problem, we see an opportunity,

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:16.576
we want to make a difference in the world.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.584
We want to make money, yes,
but we want to have an impact,

00:01:19.584 --> 00:01:22.052
we want to empower
people, we want the output

00:01:22.052 --> 00:01:25.836
that we are creating to touch
people's lives in some way.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:27.551
And I think that's the
most gratifying thing

00:01:27.551 --> 00:01:29.047
that you can do as an entrepreneur,

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:31.473
to know that the thing that you spent

00:01:31.473 --> 00:01:33.572
all this time and energy and effort

00:01:33.572 --> 00:01:36.359
in putting into the
world is being received,

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:40.083
great, people like it,
but it's empowering them

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:42.987
to do more in their lives
and in their businesses.

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:46.372
It's why my YouTube
channel is so fun for me,

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.430
it's so amazing for me to wake up

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:50.035
and see your comments everyday

00:01:50.035 --> 00:01:53.001
because I know the work
that I do is empowering,

00:01:53.001 --> 00:01:55.871
it allows you to go out and
do, hopefully, amazing things.

00:01:55.871 --> 00:01:57.645
I believe that entrepreneurs will solve

00:01:57.645 --> 00:02:00.239
every problem in the
world, the major problems.

00:02:00.239 --> 00:02:03.319
It's not big corporations,
it's entrepreneurs.

00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:06.736
And so, I can help by giving you content,

00:02:07.975 --> 00:02:09.473
by giving you inspiration,

00:02:09.473 --> 00:02:11.937
by giving you strategies and tactics

00:02:11.937 --> 00:02:15.027
to help your businesses become better.

00:02:15.027 --> 00:02:16.901
If I play a quarter percent role

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:20.421
in helping you get better
and build your company,

00:02:20.421 --> 00:02:22.325
I know it's going to
have a ripple effect out,

00:02:22.325 --> 00:02:24.824
and that's why my goal's to
help a billion entrepreneurs,

00:02:24.824 --> 00:02:26.834
because if I can touch
a billion entrepreneurs

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:30.781
in a quarter percent way,
that is massive world change.

00:02:30.781 --> 00:02:32.294
That's what gets me pumped up,

00:02:32.294 --> 00:02:33.945
that's why I love doing what I do.

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:36.182
I want to empower you
guys to do great things.

00:02:36.182 --> 00:02:38.668
If I look at this business,
Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:41.407
people come to learn how to dance salsa,

00:02:41.407 --> 00:02:43.835
but really they're
coming for other reasons,

00:02:43.835 --> 00:02:45.533
they're lonely, they want to meet people,

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:47.041
they're looking for a relationship,

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:48.283
they're looking for some friends,

00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.945
they're looking to build
their self-confidence.

00:02:49.945 --> 00:02:52.718
There's always a deeper
reason for why they come here,

00:02:52.718 --> 00:02:56.786
and people always leave feeling
happier with themselves,

00:02:56.786 --> 00:03:00.117
feeling more confident, maybe
meeting some new friends.

00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:02.466
And that empowers them
in their entire life,

00:03:02.466 --> 00:03:04.882
not just in the one hour when they come in

00:03:04.882 --> 00:03:07.634
and they learn how to do a turn, right?

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:10.494
We're empowering them
to live a better life

00:03:10.494 --> 00:03:11.536
for the rest of their life

00:03:11.536 --> 00:03:14.827
because of the time that
they spend in our class.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.663
That's exciting, that's
energizing, so we stand for.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.779
And so, if you are focused on
creating a product or service

00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:24.090
that, yes, can make
money, but has an impact

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.974
by empowering people to do great things

00:03:25.974 --> 00:03:27.597
in their lives and their businesses,

00:03:27.597 --> 00:03:29.625
I think that's the ultimate
most satisfying thing

00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.849
that you can create as an entrepreneur.

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:33.846
So the question I have
for you guys today is,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:37.450
what are you doing to empower others?

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.078
Let me know, let me feel
the passion you got for it.

00:03:40.078 --> 00:03:41.418
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:03:41.418 --> 00:03:42.621
super curious to find out.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.818
I also want to give a
quick shout to Imran Dean.

00:03:44.818 --> 00:03:46.371
Imran, thank you so much for picking up

00:03:46.371 --> 00:03:48.056
a copy of my book, "Your One Word".

00:03:48.056 --> 00:03:49.642
Really, really, really means a lot to me,

00:03:49.642 --> 00:03:51.393
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:51.393 --> 00:03:52.824
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:52.824 --> 00:03:54.158
I believe in you.

00:03:54.158 --> 00:03:56.072
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:03:56.072 --> 00:03:58.140
And remember your one word is ...

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.625
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:03:59.625 --> 00:04:02.393
for another shot of "Entspresso".

