00:04:11.287 --> 00:04:15.945
- The traditional reform
mindset towards education is

00:04:15.945 --> 00:04:18.061
let's micromanage teachers more.

00:04:18.061 --> 00:04:20.278
Like a good number of
really great teachers

00:04:20.278 --> 00:04:22.719
are getting handicapped
by this micromanaging,

00:04:22.719 --> 00:04:24.906
teaching to the test or whatever else.

00:04:24.906 --> 00:04:27.433
And forcing like, "On
Tuesday, September 27

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.619
"you have to cover this",
and you can't question that,

00:04:30.619 --> 00:04:32.115
"and you have to say it in these words",

00:04:32.115 --> 00:04:34.306
and you have no time to
run your own project,

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.214
and you have no time to
think of your own curriculum

00:04:36.214 --> 00:04:37.443
or whatever you want to do.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.823
We generally feel like the teachers

00:04:38.823 --> 00:04:40.172
are getting liberated here.

00:04:40.172 --> 00:04:41.270
Do what you want everyday

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.311
and the students are going to
learn what they want to understand

00:04:43.311 --> 00:04:46.105
and we're freeing tons of
class time for you to do

00:04:46.105 --> 00:04:48.318
what I think you wanted
to teach to begin with.

00:04:48.318 --> 00:04:50.074
Like, when I ran my little summer camp,

00:04:50.074 --> 00:04:52.501
I won't claim I have
30 years of experience

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:55.240
and all the rest, but what was fun for me

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.437
was not having to give a lecture
on least common multiple,

00:04:58.437 --> 00:05:00.704
not having to give a
lecture on probability.

00:05:00.704 --> 00:05:02.495
To know that that was out of the way

00:05:02.495 --> 00:05:04.320
and getting this super fun simulation

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.937
where the kids are trading
piece and all this,

00:05:06.937 --> 00:05:08.389
and I got to, I felt like I was able

00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:10.082
to express my creativity, I
was able to go home and say,

00:05:10.082 --> 00:05:11.360
"What would be a really cool way

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.713
"to understand this concept intuitively?"

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:16.451
And when I went to classroom
that's what we did,

00:05:16.451 --> 00:05:18.434
and I felt like it was a
much richer experience.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:21.243
And so, we genuinely feel
and we genuinely hope

00:05:21.243 --> 00:05:22.743
that it's doing that for teachers,

00:05:22.743 --> 00:05:25.602
and the teachers in Los
Altos have expressed that,

00:05:25.602 --> 00:05:27.319
that they love, the they feel liberated,

00:05:27.319 --> 00:05:29.554
they feel like they have data
that they never had before.

00:05:29.554 --> 00:05:32.853
The fifth-grade teachers
they teach all the classes,

00:05:32.853 --> 00:05:34.244
'cause they're elementary school,

00:05:34.244 --> 00:05:37.542
and they feel handicapped
in their other classes now

00:05:37.542 --> 00:05:41.376
because they are doing that, the lecture,

00:05:41.376 --> 00:05:42.883
they are doing the stuff that I would say

00:05:42.883 --> 00:05:44.955
is lower value than what they're
doing in their Math classes

00:05:44.955 --> 00:05:46.134
which is the projects,

00:05:46.134 --> 00:05:47.910
which are the one-on-one interactions.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.784
And so, they're actually asking
us as quickly as possible,

00:05:50.784 --> 00:05:53.119
"When are the grammar videos coming?

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.701
"When are the grammar exercises coming

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:55.820
"so I can do more interesting things

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.127
"with that part of my day in class?"

00:05:58.127 --> 00:06:00.627
- I've heard the story
that the first line of code

00:06:00.627 --> 00:06:02.499
that you wrote was in an
apartment in Campbell.

00:06:02.499 --> 00:06:03.581
- That's right.
- Not too far from here.

00:06:03.581 --> 00:06:04.664
- Just down the street. That's right.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.513
- I mean, did you have any idea,

00:06:06.513 --> 00:06:08.753
you know, you wrote this, you
put it out on the Internet,

00:06:08.753 --> 00:06:10.615
you didn't sort of do it thinking,

00:06:10.615 --> 00:06:12.736
"Hey, I'm going to build and
$83-billion-dollar business"?

00:06:12.736 --> 00:06:14.328
- No, of course not at all, not at all.

00:06:14.328 --> 00:06:18.590
Really, I mean, it was
just this, as I said,

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:21.035
as a software engineer I
wanted to write some tools

00:06:21.035 --> 00:06:24.488
that I thought could be
useful to ordinary people,

00:06:24.488 --> 00:06:25.738
regular people.

00:06:26.826 --> 00:06:30.993
I had a day job, started as a
nights and weekends projects.

00:06:32.439 --> 00:06:36.606
And it's amazing, of course
now, we all understand,

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.927
code does change the world and
it can change people's lives,

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.999
but I think what makes eBay unique,

00:06:46.999 --> 00:06:48.793
despite the fact there are many,

00:06:48.793 --> 00:06:51.789
so now there are more
marketplace businesses out there,

00:06:51.789 --> 00:06:56.178
we are really, have
always been about people.

00:06:56.178 --> 00:07:00.452
It's always been about bringing
tools to ordinary people.

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:04.659
And giving them the tools
and the opportunities

00:07:04.659 --> 00:07:07.175
that they need, that they can
use to then be successful,

00:07:07.175 --> 00:07:09.998
and define success in their own way.

00:07:09.998 --> 00:07:13.006
So, yeah, those were really,

00:07:13.006 --> 00:07:15.853
those were really weeks
and months for crazy.

00:07:15.853 --> 00:07:19.915
So I remember, one of
the first items listed,

00:07:19.915 --> 00:07:22.915
this was in 1995, in September 1995,

00:07:25.143 --> 00:07:26.434
one of the first items listed was

00:07:26.434 --> 00:07:29.517
a 1952 Silver Dawn Rolls-Royce, okay?

00:07:32.534 --> 00:07:35.872
And the seller, and I wish
we could find the seller,

00:07:35.872 --> 00:07:38.903
the seller was amazing because he, or she,

00:07:38.903 --> 00:07:41.346
had done this beautiful listing.

00:07:41.346 --> 00:07:44.059
And so, you know, you
could put HTML in there,

00:07:44.059 --> 00:07:46.452
the seller had created
this server somewhere

00:07:46.452 --> 00:07:47.829
to actually host photos,

00:07:47.829 --> 00:07:49.406
back in those days you
had to actually own,

00:07:49.406 --> 00:07:51.200
bring your own server to host photos,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.374
and actually had this
beautiful listing in there.

00:07:53.374 --> 00:07:55.496
I looked to that and I
said, "This is incredible.

00:07:55.496 --> 00:07:59.427
"There is no way anyone will
ever buy a car on the Internet.

00:07:59.427 --> 00:08:02.344
"Like, that's just ridiculous.
That will never happen".

00:08:02.344 --> 00:08:04.110
Of course, now there's a car sold

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.543
every four minutes on a mobile device.

00:08:06.543 --> 00:08:08.526
I mean, it's incredible,
it's totally incredible.

00:08:08.526 --> 00:08:10.806
So, who could have imagines that?

00:08:10.806 --> 00:08:14.806
- How do you motivate
people to get things done?

00:08:21.742 --> 00:08:24.630
- You know, the reason why I paused was

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.630
I was trying not to come
up with a tried answer.

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:34.300
I think, and this is a
much use, an overused term,

00:08:35.303 --> 00:08:39.303
I think defining an overall
goal that's reaching

00:08:42.876 --> 00:08:46.425
in that it isn't attainable,
and then empowering,

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.475
this is the overused word,
and then empowering people

00:08:49.475 --> 00:08:51.975
to actually go try and get it,

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.545
and ensuring that when they have a misstep

00:08:56.545 --> 00:08:59.714
that you're there to help them along

00:08:59.714 --> 00:09:01.540
is probably the way to.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.252
I mean, you know, to be frank with you,

00:09:03.252 --> 00:09:05.801
most of the people that we
hired are extremely smart,

00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:08.852
they're self-motivated,
they're very hardworking,

00:09:08.852 --> 00:09:12.899
and you've got to, much like a racehorse,

00:09:12.899 --> 00:09:16.067
you've got to make sure
that you give them the space

00:09:16.067 --> 00:09:19.150
to develop and mature and accomplish.

00:09:20.776 --> 00:09:25.148
So I think most of my partners
would say the same thing.

00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:28.154
I mean, it takes an element of defining

00:09:28.154 --> 00:09:30.520
the ultimate destination
and then empowering people

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.600
to actually go to achieve it.

